---
import Answer from "../../components/challenge/Answer.astro";
import ChallengeIntro from "../../components/challenge/ChallengeIntro.astro";
import Checklist from "../../components/challenge/Checklist.astro";
import Message from "../../components/challenge/Message.astro";
import Task from "../../components/challenge/Task.astro";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Online Research - AI Training Guide">
	<PageShell chapterId="exploring-ai-capabilities" subChapterId="online-research">
		<ChallengeIntro skill="The agent can research a topic online and write it up as a report, with every claim linked to where it came from.">
			The claims fraud team keeps getting phone claims that blame fictional kaiju. They want a reference their handlers can check a
			claim against, and a check that none of our own kaiju share a name with a fictional one.
		</ChallengeIntro>

		<Message kind="email" subject="Fictional kaiju reference" from="Claims Fraud Team" to="Web Team" date="Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:20">
			<p>
				Phone claims keep blaming Godzilla. Handlers need a reference of fictional kaiju, from films, TV, anime and games, so they
				can spot a claim that names one. Include anything from the last couple of years; that's what people quote now.
			</p>
			<p>
				While you're at it, check none of our kaiju share a name with a fictional one. We'd rather know before a journalist does.
			</p>
		</Message>

		<Task>Write a prompt to have your agent research fictional kaiju online and produce an HTML report the fraud team can use.</Task>

		<Checklist
			items={[
				"Cover fictional kaiju from at least four franchises.",
				"Give each one its name and aliases, where and when it first appeared, its height and what it looks like.",
				"Include entries from the last two years.",
				"Link every entry to its source.",
				"Say which source it trusted when sources disagree.",
				"Compare our own kaiju against the fictional ones and list any name clashes or near-misses.",
				"Produce the whole thing as an HTML report.",
			]}
		/>

		<Answer
			prompt={`Research fictional kaiju online, from films, TV, anime and games, including anything from the last two years. Search for each one rather than relying on memory.

For each entry give its name and aliases, where and when it first appeared, its height and what it looks like, with a link to the source you used. When sources disagree, say which one you trusted.

Then get our own kaiju from the API or the admin portal and check them for name clashes or near-misses with the fictional ones.

Produce an HTML report our claims handlers can use to spot a claim that names a fictional kaiju.`}
		>
			<p>
				An agent can list the famous kaiju from memory without searching. The "last two years" rule and the per-entry sources are
				there to force real searches. Check the report by clicking three source links, and ask the agent where a recent entry came
				from. A made-up or dead link is the failure to look for.
			</p>
			<p>
				Our kaiju are Old Gullet, Cinderback, Meridian, Thornmaw, Vessa and Pellucid. A good agent reads them from the app instead
				of guessing, then checks each one.
			</p>
			<p>Fan wikis often disagree on heights and first appearances. A good report says which source it went with.</p>
		</Answer>
	</PageShell>
</MainLayout>
